this is the fix. If the component is already non-bipartite, we don't need to record anything.\n\nLet me update the code.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. Is it possible for a component to become non-bipartite and then become bipartite again (without any rollback)? No, because adding edges can only make things worse (or keep them the same). Removing edges could make a non-bipartite component bipartite again, but in our offline approach, we handle removals via rollback.\n\nSo the fix is correct: only push to history if the component was previously bipartite.\n\nLet me update the union function:\n\n```python\ndef union(u, v):\n    par = parent\n    par_ = parity\n    rnk = rank\n    bip = is_bip\n    hist = history\n    \n    ru = u\n    pu = 0\n    while par[ru] != ru:\n        pu ^= par_[ru]\n        ru = par[ru]\n    \n    rv = v\n    pv = 0\n    while par[rv] != rv:\n        pv ^= par_[rv]\n        rv = par[rv]\n    \n    if ru == rv:\n        if (pu ^ pv) != 1 and bip[ru]:\n            hist.append((0, ru))\n            bip[ru] = False\n        else:\n            hist.append((0, -1))\n    else:\n        if rnk[ru] > rnk[rv]:\n            ru, rv = rv, ru\n            pu, pv = pv, pu\n        \n        hist.append((1, ru, rv, par[ru], rnk[rv], par_[ru], bip[ru], bip[rv]))\n        \n        par[ru] = rv\n        par_[ru] = pu ^ pv ^ 1\n        bip[rv] = bip[ru] and bip[rv]\n        if rnk[ru] == rnk[rv]:\n            rnk[rv] += 1\n```\n\nGood. Now the code should be correct.\n\nLet me write the final version with all fixes:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    n = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    q = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    if q == 0:\n        return\n    \n    ops = [None] * q\n    active_edges = {}\n    edge_intervals = []\n    \n    for t in range(q):\n        op = data[idx]; idx += 1\n        u = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n        v = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n        \n        if op == 